# Mocking Sprite: "Instant and sorcery spells you cast cost {1} less to cast" (CR 601.2f, 118.7a). Bot1 casts it with Black Lotus's
# {U}{U}{U}, then has a lone Mox Sapphire. Burrog Befuddler ({1}{U}, a creature spell) is not reduced and is refused; Opt ({1}{U}, an
# instant) costs {U} and is paid by the Sapphire alone. On turn 3 Energize ({1}{U}, a sorcery) costs {U} too: the Sapphire pays it with
# nothing else untapped and Bot2's Ornithopter goes back to Bot2's hand.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mocking Sprite
Mox Sapphire
Opt
Burrog Befuddler
Energize
Island
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Mocking Sprite.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
! Bot1.Hand.Burrog Befuddler.Cast(Mana: short)
Bot1.Hand.Opt.Cast
? Bot1.Mana =
Bot1.Arrange(Island |)
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Energize.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
? Bot1.Mana =
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

